      "snowpackStructure": {
        "comment": "Forecast Weather Influences: Gale force South-South-East winds will decrease only slightly overnight, continuing  very strong throughout the period. \r\nHeavy snowfall overnight will ease to become patchy and light during the day. A complex freezing level with summit temperatures on average around -3.5 Celsius.\nObserved Weather Influences: Gale force South-South-East winds. Snow showers during the morning eased to become mostly dry during the afternoon. Snow initially falling to lower elevations, then became confined to above around 750 metres. The freezing level was 1000 metres.\nObservedSnowStability: Unstable windslab is lying on West through North to North-East aspects above 1000 metres. The greatest instabilities are in steep locations such as gullies, gully exits, coire rims and convexities. On these aspects, fragile cornices are present. The avalanche hazard is Moderate."
